      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “vitality” as “available psychological energy” or as a “sense of being energized”; it only discusses that effortful defensive/emotion-regulation processes may require more energy resources and could be accompanied by “impaired vitality.”",
        "The definition’s framing (“available psychological energy or sense of being energized”) goes beyond what is directly supported in the provided packet text.",
        "While parts of the definition about stress/effortful defensive or emotion-regulation processes contributing to depleted resources are broadly consistent with the packet (e.g., effortful emotion regulation and the idea of higher energy/cognitive load linked to impaired vitality), the unsupported characterization of what vitality specifically refers to prevents passing."
